alacritty_terminal on powerpc-apple-darwin (Mac OS X 10.6.8): `[ERROR] [alacritty_terminal] Event loop registration
error: Invalid argument (os error 22)` at startup, then a terminal that never reads or writes its pty (alacritty 0.17.0:
window and red message bar, no reaction to input). The pty master fd is registered with the `polling` crate, i.e. kqueue
on macOS, and 10.6's kernel has no kqueue filter for tty devices (`spec_kqfilter` knows only bpf; `filt_specattach` for
ttys came with 10.7), so kevent answers EINVAL; Darwin's poll(2) takes no devices either, select(2) does. On PowerPC the
pty is watched by a "PTY select relay" thread: select(2) on the master, one token into a socketpair the poller watches
under PTY_READ_WRITE_TOKEN, re-armed when the event loop's reader takes the token; the reader and writer are dups of the
pty fd (a write that would block waits with select(2); when alacritty asks for writable interest the socketpair is
always writable, so the pending output is flushed at once and the interest dropped). Nothing changes on other targets.

